oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome success
file Makefile kept 4
| # The halves are spelt against the directory the command runs in, exactly as
| # the whole list is: a recursive child names its prerequisites the way its own
| # Makefile did, so `$(?D)` is `d .` there and never `sub/d sub`.
| all: ; @$(MAKE) -C sub
file sub/Makefile kept 2
| out: d/a b
| 	@printf 'q=[%s] D=[%s] F=[%s]\n' '$?' '$(?D)' '$(?F)' > out
file sub/b kept 1
| b
file sub/d/a kept 1
| a
file sub/out touched 1
| q=[d/a b] D=[d .] F=[a b]
